Before proceeding to the next development stage, perform a thorough review of the current implementation.

1. Inspect all newly created and modified files.
2. Check for duplicate components, unnecessary dependencies and poor code organization.
3. Run the frontend and backend.
4. Run all relevant automated tests.
5. Check browser console errors and backend terminal errors.
6. Verify API integration and MongoDB persistence.
7. Check responsive behavior on desktop, tablet and mobile.
8. Identify incomplete functionality and security problems.
9. Fix all critical issues before declaring the stage complete.

Provide a concise development report containing:
- Files created or modified.
- Features implemented.
- Tests executed and their results.
- Known bugs or incomplete features.
- Commands required to run the application.

Do not begin the next stage until I approve it.